  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-09-30T23:09:25.271Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Why do we not have the option for certain avatar toggles to be local only? There are many toggleable functions on my avatar that don't need to be networked at all, yet I still need to add them to my parameters list to have them in my expressions menu.\nA good example is VRCLens. That is a prefab that doesnt need to be networked at all. Also a lot of my OSC integrations are local only such as having a mute toggle for discord on my avatar, immobilize toggle etc. These do not need to be networked to other players but I dont have the option for it to be local only. People have HUD's etc built into their avatars that only need to be local only. I could probably save 30+ bits of parameter memory if OSC and the expression menu could interface with local only parameters. Please make this an option, thank you.",
